<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nachan Kaan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">early 16th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nachan Kaan was the Maya lord of Chetumal, on the south-east coast of the Yucatán peninsula, at the time of the Spanish conquest. The shipwrecked Spaniard <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gonzalo-guerrero">Gonzalo Guerrero</a> married his daughter, adopted Maya customs and led Chetumal's warriors against Spanish expeditions. Their children are often described as among the first people of mixed Spanish and Maya descent.</p></div>
